hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-41 = unlines (cons "*Singular* returns at the end of the reading because the seed, the hyperactive kernel, is singular. One kernel, one reaction, one root for *same* and *simple* and *singular*. *Simple* is *sem* + *plek*, folded once. A simple thing is folded once; a complex thing, *com* + *plectere*, is braided together. *Perplex* is braided through. The work's design is simple in the oldest sense: everything is folded once around one root, and the complexity is the braiding of that one fold with itself. The interaction net is a braid. DNA is a braid. Text is a weave. A language of languages is the braid of tongues. Hyperactive Interaction is the name for the fold that, folded once more, is everything else." nil)
